    {
      "id": "p0016-b003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "The word \"localization\" is actually relatively new in the translation world, so different people use it to mean different things. Here's how I would define it in simple terms, though:",
        "raw": "The word \"localization\" is actually relatively new in the translation world, so\ndifferent people use it to mean different things. Here's how I would define it in\nsimple terms, though:",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29155822,
          0.14652143,
          0.89154508,
          0.19497857
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.28458362,
          0.14580714,
          0.90030881,
          0.19605
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          4,
          5,
          6
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "“本地化”在翻译界其实还是个相对年轻的词，不同的人用它表达不同的意思。简单来说，我会这样定义：",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
      "annotations": [],
